# FRONTEND - PUBLIC VALUES ONLY.
# Every NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable is inlined into the JavaScript bundle at BUILD
# time and is visible to anyone who opens the site. Never put a secret here
# (no JWT secret, database URL, API key, or Setu credential - those belong to
# the backend only). Locally: copy to .env.local (gitignored). Staging: set it
# in the hosting platform's build environment, then rebuild - changing it
# after the build has no effect. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
#
# Set exactly ONE of the two variables below (the build fails if both are set).
#
# Direct mode (local dev): the browser calls the backend at this origin.
# Scheme + host (+ port) only, no trailing slash, no /api/v1 (request paths
# already include it). Must share a hostname with the frontend (localhost,
# not 127.0.0.1) so session cookies are shared. Defaults to
# http://localhost:8000 when neither variable is set.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
#
# Proxy mode (deployments where the frontend and backend have unrelated
# domains, e.g. *.vercel.app + *.onrender.com): the frontend reverse-proxies
# /api/* to this origin and the browser only ever calls its own origin, so
# the session survives a page reload. NOT a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable - it is
# read only by next.config.ts at build time and never reaches the browser
# bundle. https:// only, scheme + host only. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
# BACKEND_ORIGIN=https://CHANGE_ME.onrender.com
